---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---

<section class="section section--alt" id="network">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head section-head--center">
      <p class="eyebrow">Built for real networks</p>
      <h2 class="h2">It connects where other apps don't.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Serafim was built for people on mobile networks that block the usual
        hosting providers, and for the cheap Android Go phones that other apps
        already skip. Those are design constraints, not afterthoughts.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="net">
      <div class="net__path reveal">
        <div class="net__node">
          <span class="net__icon"><Icon name="phone" size={18} /></span>
          <span class="net__name">Your phone</span>
          <span class="net__desc">Message stored locally first</span>
        </div>

        <span class="net__link"><span class="net__link-line"></span></span>

        <div class="net__node">
          <span class="net__icon"><Icon name="signal" size={18} /></span>
          <span class="net__name">Edge network</span>
          <span class="net__desc">Reachable on any operator</span>
        </div>

        <span class="net__link"><span class="net__link-line"></span></span>

        <div class="net__node">
          <span class="net__icon"><Icon name="server" size={18} /></span>
          <span class="net__name">Serafim API</span>
          <span class="net__desc">Realtime messages and accounts</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="net__grid">
        <article class="card reveal">
          <div class="card__icon"><Icon name="signal" /></div>
          <h3 class="h4">Fronted by an edge network</h3>
          <p>
            The app's API sits behind a CDN edge, because some mobile networks
            block the addresses its host is published on. If you have ever seen
            "can't reach the server" on a chat app, this is the fix.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card reveal">
          <div class="card__icon"><Icon name="android" /></div>
          <h3 class="h4">One APK, both architectures</h3>
          <p>
            A single download covers 32-bit and 64-bit phones, so the cheap
            itel and Android Go devices in the market can install it too. You
            can never grab the wrong file.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card reveal">
          <div class="card__icon"><Icon name="bolt" /></div>
          <h3 class="h4">Local-first, not server-first</h3>
          <p>
            Messages are written to the phone's own database and then synced.
            The app opens straight to your chat list, and conversations still
            open when the network drops.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card reveal">
          <div class="card__icon"><Icon name="image" /></div>
          <h3 class="h4">Shrink before you send</h3>
          <p>
            Photos are resized on the device before they go anywhere. Pick
            data saver, standard or high quality and Serafim does the rest
            before it touches your data bundle.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .net__path {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .net__node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 220px;
    padding: 1.2rem 1rem;
    background: var(--paper-alt);
    border: var(--bw) solid var(--line);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .net__icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 38px;
    height: 38px;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border: var(--bw) solid var(--line);
    color: var(--primary-pale);
  }

  .net__name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .net__desc {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .net__link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    width: clamp(18px, 5vw, 60px);
  }

  .net__link-line {
    width: 100%;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--primary);
  }

  .net__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .net__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .net__path {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .net__node {
      max-width: none;
    }

    .net__link {
      width: 100%;
      height: 22px;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .net__link-line {
      width: 2px;
      height: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
